      "scope": "Three or more fresh runs of the actual previously timed direct-counting C/Rust/fwp binaries, on the matching native architecture. GNU time records whole-process peak RSS in KiB, including startup, output and shutdown. Separate balanced rotating/reversed timing rounds record whole-process elapsed and child user+system CPU time with explicit warmups/sample count. Elapsed includes Python subprocess launch, input/output and shutdown; child CPU excludes parent and descheduled time. No recompilation occurs inside either timed interval. Every sample is retained. These memory runs are excluded from the timing comparison; RSS includes shared code/libraries and has page/accounting granularity. Separate instrumented GCC O2 builds of saved fwp C count managed requests, retains and peak/final charged bytes after constant initialization through cleanup. They exclude raw buffers, allocator metadata, stacks and libc. A single injected 16-byte leaf allocation must be detected. No C/Rust allocator-call count or peak-RSS improvement over older fwp is claimed."
